<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gajpat Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1738–1789</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gajpat Singh was a Phulkian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> chief who seized Jind and surrounding territory around 1763 after the fall of Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a>, founding the Jind State. He received the title of raja from the Mughal emperor in 1772. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> Kaur married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maha-singh">Maha Singh</a> and was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p></div>
